1
00:00:00,130 --> 00:00:02,130
Good evening, excellence…

2
00:00:02,610 --> 00:00:04,230
The most expensive thing on site…

3
00:00:04,240 --> 00:00:05,530
is the cheap thing!

4
00:00:05,990 --> 00:00:07,496
A contractor saved an hour

5
00:00:07,496 --> 00:00:08,700
checking the roof rebar…

6
00:00:09,020 --> 00:00:10,920
and the consultant rejected the pour.

7
00:00:11,440 --> 00:00:13,950
The visible cost? Concrete and labor.

8
00:00:13,950 --> 00:00:15,280
But under the water…

9
00:00:15,580 --> 00:00:16,810
there's an iceberg:

10
00:00:16,830 --> 00:00:18,270
schedule delays,

11
00:00:18,390 --> 00:00:19,290
penalties,

12
00:00:19,290 --> 00:00:20,600
overtime,

13
00:00:20,680 --> 00:00:22,700
and a client whose trust was shaken.

14
00:00:22,980 --> 00:00:23,750
This is called

15
00:00:23,750 --> 00:00:25,550
the Cost of Poor Quality

16
00:00:25,850 --> 00:00:29,050
The American Society for Quality says

17
00:00:29,210 --> 00:00:31,060
that in many companies it reaches

18
00:00:31,060 --> 00:00:33,530
15 or 20 percent

19
00:00:33,620 --> 00:00:35,010
of sales

20
00:00:35,230 --> 00:00:36,640
The famous rule:

21
00:00:37,070 --> 00:00:39,320
one, ten, a hundred:

22
00:00:39,600 --> 00:00:41,440
a pound to prevent the mistake…

23
00:00:41,440 --> 00:00:43,340
ten to fix it internally…

24
00:00:43,340 --> 00:00:44,385
and a hundred if

25
00:00:44,385 --> 00:00:45,430
it reaches the client.

26
00:00:45,560 --> 00:00:46,840
Remember it this way:

27
00:00:47,320 --> 00:00:48,530
The cheap mistake…

28
00:00:48,530 --> 00:00:50,020
turns out the most expensive.

29
00:00:50,270 --> 00:00:51,853
And you? What's the costliest

30
00:00:51,853 --> 00:00:53,120
small mistake you've seen?

31
00:00:53,120 --> 00:00:54,740
Write it in the comments

32
00:00:55,190 --> 00:00:56,550
See you tomorrow…

33
00:00:56,750 --> 00:00:58,330
on Masaa Al-Tamayoz
